{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 17,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Better is a dry morsel, and quietness therewith,\nThan a house full of feasting with strife.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A servant that dealeth wisely shall have rule over a son that causeth shame,\nAnd shall have part in the inheritance among the brethren.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The refining pot is for silver, and the furnace for gold;\nBut Jehovah trieth the hearts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "An evil-doer giveth heed to wicked lips;",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "And",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a liar giveth ear to a mischievous tongue.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoso mocketh the poor reproacheth his Maker;",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "And",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that is glad at calamity shall not be unpunished.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Children’s children are the crown of old men;\nAnd the glory of children are their fathers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Excellent speech becometh not a fool;\nMuch less do lying lips a prince.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A bribe is ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a precious stone in the eyes of him that hath it;\nWhithersoever it turneth, it prospereth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that covereth a transgression seeketh love;\nBut he that harpeth on a matter separateth chief friends.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A rebuke entereth deeper into one that hath understanding\nThan a hundred stripes into a fool.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "An evil man seeketh only rebellion;\nTherefore a cruel messenger shall be sent against him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let a bear robbed of her whelps meet a man,\nRather than a fool in his folly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Whoso rewardeth evil for good,\nEvil shall not depart from his house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The beginning of strife is ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " when one letteth out water:\nTherefore leave off contention, before there is quarrelling.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that justifieth the wicked, and he that condemneth the righteous,\nBoth of them alike are an abomination to Jehovah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wherefore is there a price in the hand of a fool to buy wisdom,\nSeeing he hath no understanding?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A friend loveth at all times;\nAnd a brother is born for adversity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A man void of understanding striketh hands,\nAnd becometh surety in the presence of his neighbor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He loveth transgression that loveth strife:\nHe that raiseth high his gate seeketh destruction.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that hath a wayward heart findeth no good;\nAnd he that hath a perverse tongue falleth into mischief.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that begetteth a fool ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "doeth it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to his sorrow;\nAnd the father of a fool hath no joy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A cheerful heart is a good medicine;\nBut a broken spirit drieth up the bones.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A wicked man receiveth a bribe out of the bosom,\nTo pervert the ways of justice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Wisdom is before the face of him that hath understanding;\nBut the eyes of a fool are in the ends of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A foolish son is a grief to his father,\nAnd bitterness to her that bare him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also to punish the righteous is not good,",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nor",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to smite the noble for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " uprightness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He that spareth his words hath knowledge;\nAnd he that is of a cool spirit is a man of understanding.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.17.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PRO.17.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even a fool, when he holdeth his peace, is counted wise;When he shutteth his lips, he is ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "esteemed as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " prudent.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
